INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (18, 'en', 0, 'ref-see-also', 'See also', '- Automating tasks with scripts');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (18, 'en', 1, 'ref-options', 'Options', '- Indefinitely pauses the script until the user clicks Continue (a button created by FileMaker Pro in the status toolbar) or presses Enter.

- For duration pauses the script for the number of seconds you specify.');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (18, 'en', 2, 'ref-orig', 'Originated in version', '6.0 or earlier');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (18, 'en', 3, 'ref-desc', 'Description', 'This script step can, for example, wait for a user to enter data, and then guide the user from screen to screen, prompting for data entry as needed. You can also use Pause/Resume Script to help debug your scripts, for example, to see what value is in a field at a particular point in a script or to evaluate the progress of a script.

The Pause/Resume Script script step operates on the foreground window of the file from which the script is performed. If the script''s current window is hidden, Pause/Resume Script brings that window to the front and shows it.

The For duration value must evaluate as a number, which is the duration of the pause in seconds. If you use the Specify Calculation dialog box to determine the duration, the calculation result must be a number or your script will not pause.

To give you more control over a user''s actions when a script pauses, FileMaker Pro makes some menu commands unavailable to users. You can define buttons to let users perform actions not available on the menus.');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (18, 'en', 4, 'notes', 'Notes', '- A Pause/Resume Script script step unfreezes a Freeze Window script step.

- In FileMaker WebDirect, if the Pause/Resume Script step pauses a script and the web user is idle for longer than the session timeout specified in Admin Console for FileMaker Server or FileMaker Cloud, the web user''s connection closes and the script ends early, which may lead to unexpected results.

- In Custom Web Publishing and the FileMaker Data API, this script step is supported, but you should avoid using it. If the script remains in a paused state until the session times out, then the script will not be completed.');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (18, 'en', 5, 'ref-example1', 'Example 1', 'Goes to the Print Invoices layout and pauses. The user can click a Continue button on the status toolbar or the layout to print the records.

Copy

Go to Layout ["Print Invoices"]
Pause/Resume Script [Indefinitely]
Print [Restore: Printer; With dialog: Off]
Go to Layout [original layout]');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (18, 'en', 6, 'related', 'Related topics', '- Script steps reference

- About formulas');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (19, 'en', 0, 'ref-see-also', 'See also', '- Automating tasks with scripts');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (19, 'en', 1, 'ref-options', 'Options', '- Specified:

- From list allows you to select the script you want to perform.

- By name allows you to specify the script name by a calculation. The script name is not case sensitive.

- Parameter specifies a script parameter for the specified script.');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (19, 'en', 2, 'ref-orig', 'Originated in version', '6.0 or earlier');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (19, 'en', 3, 'ref-desc', 'Description', 'There is no need to open an external file when using a script in it—FileMaker Pro opens it for you.

You can use separate scripts to break complex tasks into smaller segments, which are often easier to troubleshoot. You can also save time by putting common tasks like printing or exporting records into separate scripts, which can then be accessed by more than one script. For example, you might want to use the same page setup and printing options in several scripts. By defining those steps once and saving them in separate scripts, you make it easy to access those steps many times.

Use script parameters to pass text or numbers into a script. When a parameter is specified, that parameter may be accessed within a script or passed to other script steps using the Get(ScriptParameter) function.

Script parameters:

- exist within the parent script only unless explicitly passed to the sub-script. If your script calls another script, parameters in the called script are independent of parameters in the parent script.

- exist only for the duration of the script. Script parameters are reset each time a script is performed.

- can be used (but not modified) within a script and can be passed along to sub-scripts by using the Get(ScriptParameter) function as the parameter for the sub-script. You can also specify different parameters each time the sub-script is called using Perform Script. Changing the parameters passed to a sub-script does not modify the value of the parameters returned from Get(ScriptParameter) in the parent script.

- can contain multiple values separated by carriage returns. Use the LeftValues function, MiddleValues function, and RightValues function to isolate a specific parameter.

Tip If you''ve performed an external script and you want to return to the original file, add an Enter Browse Mode step or Go to Layout step right after the Perform Script step in the original file, so that the script returns to the original file.');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (19, 'en', 4, 'notes', 'Notes', '- If you use By name to specify a script in another FileMaker Pro file, the calculation must evaluate to <data source name>::<script name>, such as "Invoices::Do Quarterly Billing." Both data source and script names are case sensitive.

- If you are defining a custom menu item that performs a script, select the script and optional script parameters. See Defining custom menus.

- For scripts run via FileMaker WebDirect, the FileMaker Data API, and Custom Web Publishing, the files containing the scripts must be on the same host and have the appropriate extended privileges enabled to permit access. See Editing extended privileges for a privilege set.');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (19, 'en', 5, 'ref-example1', 'Example 1', 'Runs the "Print Invoice Report" script with no parameters.

Copy

Go to Layout ["Invoice Report"]
Perform Script [Specified: From list; "Print Invoice Report"; Parameter: ]');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (19, 'en', 6, 'ref-examplen', 'Example 2', 'Uses a field value, Customer Name, as the parameter. Invoices for the current customer are returned in a new window with the Invoice Report layout.

Main script: Current Customer Invoices

Copy

Find Matching Records [Replace; Invoices::Customer ID]
#Calls the "View Customer Invoices" sub-script defined below
Perform Script [Specified: From list; "View Customer Invoices"; Parameter: Invoices::Customer Name]

Sub-script: View Customer Invoices

Copy

New Window [Style: Document; Name: "Customer: " & Get ( ScriptParameter ); Using layout: "Invoice Report" (Invoices)]
Sort Records [Restore; With dialog: Off]');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (19, 'en', 7, 'ref-examplen', 'Example 3', 'Shows a custom dialog box with the default button and button 2, then performs the script named "Button1" or "Button2" depending on the user''s choice returned in Get ( LastMessageChoice ).

Copy

Show Custom Dialog [ "Do you want to continue?" ]
Perform Script [ Specified: By name ; "Button" & Get ( LastMessageChoice ) ; Parameter: ]');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (19, 'en', 8, 'related', 'Related topics', '- Perform Script and script parameter examples

- Script steps reference

- About formulas');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (20, 'en', 0, 'ref-see-also', 'See also', '- Automating tasks with scripts');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (20, 'en', 1, 'ref-options', 'Options', '- Specified:

- From list allows you to select the script you want to perform.

- By name allows you to specify the script name by a calculation. The script name is not case sensitive.

- Parameter specifies a script parameter for the specified script.

- Wait for completion pauses the script on the client until the sub-script called by Perform Script On Server is completed on the host. Wait for completion must be selected to pass a script result or error code from the host to the client. Use the Get(ScriptResult) function to capture a result or the Get(LastError) function to capture an error code.');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (20, 'en', 2, 'ref-orig', 'Originated in version', '13.0');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (20, 'en', 3, 'ref-desc', 'Description', 'The current file must be hosted on FileMaker Server or FileMaker Cloud. Otherwise, Perform Script On Server returns an error. See About running scripts on FileMaker Server and FileMaker Cloud.');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (20, 'en', 4, 'notes', 'Notes', '-
If you use By name to specify a script in another FileMaker Pro file, the calculation must evaluate to <data source name>::<script name>, such as "Invoices::Do Quarterly Billing." Both data source and script names are case sensitive.

-
Because this script step can itself be performed by a server-side script, take care to avoid scenarios that might cause dead locks or infinite loops—for example, script A calls script B, which calls script A—adversely affecting server performance.');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (20, 'en', 5, 'ref-example1', 'Example 1', 'Runs a script on the server and sends the current layout name, customer ID, and customer email address as the script parameter. The server navigates to the layout and record specified in the parameter, saves a snapshot link of the current record, emails the snapshot link to the email address specified in the parameter, and returns a result. The client fetches the script result from the server and displays it in a custom dialog box.

Main script: Email snapshot link (Client)

Copy

Perform Script on Server [Specified: From list ; "Email snapshot link (Server)" ; Parameter: List ( Get ( LayoutName ) ; Customers::ID ; Customers::Email ) ; Wait for completion: On]
Show Custom Dialog [Get ( ScriptResult )]

Sub-script: Email snapshot link (Server)

Copy

Go to Layout [GetValue ( Get ( ScriptParameter ) ; 1 )]
Enter Find Mode [Pause: Off]
Set Field [Customers::ID; GetValue ( Get ( ScriptParameter ) ; 2 )]
Perform Find [ ]
Set Variable [$PATH; Value:Get ( TemporaryPath ) & "Snapshot.fmpsl"]
Save Records as Snapshot Link ["$PATH"; Current record ; Create folders: Off]
Send Mail [Send via SMTP Server; With dialog: Off; To: GetValue ( Get ( ScriptParameter ) ; 3 ); "$PATH"]
Exit Script [Text Result: "Snapshot link sent."]');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (20, 'en', 6, 'related', 'Related topics', '- Perform Script script step

- Perform Script and script parameter examples

- Script steps reference');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (21, 'en', 0, 'ref-see-also', 'See also', '-
Automating tasks with scripts');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (21, 'en', 1, 'ref-options', 'Options', '-
Specified:

-
From list allows you to select the script you want to perform.

-
By name allows you to specify the script name by a calculation. The script name is not case sensitive.

-
Parameter specifies a script parameter for the specified script.

-
Callback script specified is the script to run on the client after the script is completed on the server. Choose:

-
From list allows you to select the script you want to perform.

-
By name allows you to specify the script name by a calculation. The script name is not case sensitive.

-
Parameter specifies a script parameter for the specified callback script.

-
State specifies how to handle a currently running script when the callback script is run. The options are Continue, Halt, Exit, Resume, and Pause. See Options for handling the current script when starting new scripts.');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (21, 'en', 2, 'ref-orig', 'Originated in version', '20.1');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (21, 'en', 3, 'ref-desc', 'Description', 'The current file must be hosted on FileMaker Server or FileMaker Cloud. Otherwise, this script step returns an error. See About running scripts on FileMaker Server and FileMaker Cloud.

The callback script is scheduled to run on the client after any current script has been completed, just like scripts that are triggered by the Install OnTimer Script script step and the OnWindowTransaction script trigger. The context in which the script runs is unknown and cannot be depended on to be the same as when this script step was executed. If needed, use the callback script''s parameter to pass back enough context for it to run as expected on the client, such as the layout and found set to use.

Note If you specify a calculation as a parameter in the callback script, the calculation will be evaluated when the callback script runs on the client.

In the below example, nothing would be returned because $data does not exist when the callback script is executed on the client.

-
Caller

Set Variable [ $data ; Value: 1 ]

Perform Script on Server with Callback [ Specified: From list ; "Test" ; Parameter: ; Callback script specified: From list ; "Callback" ; Parameter: $data ; State: Continue ]

-
Test

Set Variable [ $data ; Value: 2 ]

-
Callback

Set Variable [ $param ; Value: Get ( ScriptParameter ) ]

Show Custom Dialog [ $param ]');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (21, 'en', 4, 'notes', 'Notes', '-
The callback script will not be called in the following scenarios:

-
The server or client quits unexpectedly.

-
The user quits the client or closes the file before the script on the server is completed.

-
The network connection is lost while the script step is being executed. However, reconnecting within 10 minutes after the server script is completed causes the callback script to be executed.

-
Multiple instances of this script step can be run consecutively. The callback scripts run in the order that these script steps complete.

-
If a callback script is not specified, this script step will run similarly to the Perform Script on Server script step.

-
The value of the Parameter option for the specified callback script is evaluated when the callback script is performed, which could be much later than when the server-side script is run. When the expression for the Parameter option is evaluated for the callback script, Get(ScriptParameter) and Get(ScriptResult) will have no value, because a callback script is never started while another script is running and does not inherit the calling script''s context. To specify a value for the callback script to use later, use a constant, a global field, a global (not local) variable, or a calculation using functions other than Get(ScriptParameter) or Get(ScriptResult) in this script step''s Parameter option for the specified callback script.

-
To pass a value from the calling script to the callback script, you can include the value as part of the server-side script''s parameter and return it from the server-side script using the Exit Script script step. The callback script can then retrieve it using Get(ScriptResult). See Example 1.');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (21, 'en', 5, 'ref-example1', 'Example 1', 'Runs a script on the server and sends the current layout name, customer ID, and customer email address as the script parameter. The server navigates to the layout and record specified in the parameter, saves a snapshot link of the current record, emails the snapshot link to the email address specified in the parameter, and returns a result. The client fetches the script result from the server and displays it in a custom dialog box. To use the server script''s result in the callback script, note that the callback script itself uses Get(ScriptResult), which returns the value passed by the server script''s Exit Script script step.

Main script: Email snapshot link (Client)

Copy

Perform Script on Server with Callback [ Specified: From list ; "Email snapshot link (Server)" ;
Parameter: List ( Get ( LayoutName ) ; Customers::ID ; Customers::Email ) ;
Callback script specified: From list ; "Complete message (Client)" ; Parameter: ; State: Continue ]

Sub-script: Email snapshot link (Server)

Copy

Go to Layout [ GetValue ( Get ( ScriptParameter ) ; 1 ) ; Animation: None ]
Enter Find Mode [ Pause: Off ]
Set Field [ Customers::ID ; GetValue ( Get ( ScriptParameter ) ; 2 ) ]
Perform Find [ ]
Set Variable [ $PATH ; Value: Get ( TemporaryPath ) & "Snapshot.fmpsl" ]
Save Records as Snapshot Link [ "$PATH" ; Current record ; Create folders: Off ]
Send Mail [ Send via SMTP Server ; No dialog ; To: GetValue ( Get ( ScriptParameter ) ; 3 ) ; "$PATH" ]
Exit Script [ Text Result: "Snapshot link sent." ]

Callback script: Complete message (Client)

Copy

Show Custom Dialog [ Get ( ScriptResult ) ]');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (21, 'en', 6, 'related', 'Related topics', '-
Perform Script On Server script step

