INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (148, 'en', 0, 'ref-see-also', 'See also', '- Automating tasks with scripts');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (148, 'en', 1, 'ref-options', 'Options', '-
Account Name is a text expression for the name of the AI account to use. In the current file, use the Configure AI Account script step to set up the account and assign it this name any time before this script step runs.

-
Embedding Model is the name of the model to generate embedding vectors. Specify the model name as a text expression. For supported models, see FileMaker technical specifications.

-
Input is any expression that returns text or container data to send to the model for conversion to embedding vectors.

-
Parameters is a text expression for a JSON object that consists of key-value pairs for additional parameters that are supported by the model provider. For example: {"dimension": 512}.

Note Refer to the model provider''s documentation for the parameters and values supported by the model you''re using.

-
Target specifies the field or variable to insert the returned embedding vectors into. If the variable doesn''t exist, this script step creates it (see Using variables). If you specify a text field or a variable, the returned data is stored as text. If you specify a container field, then the returned data is stored as binary data, which can be smaller than when stored as text and can improve performance in any further processing with the embedding vectors.');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (148, 'en', 2, 'ref-orig', 'Originated in version', '21.0');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (148, 'en', 3, 'ref-desc', 'Description', 'One example of how you might use embedding vectors is with the Perform Semantic Find script step, which can query the vector data produced by this script step or the Insert Embedding in Found Set script step.

For image as well as text embedding vectors, you can use the models supported by Claris AI Model Server. See the Configuring AI services in FileMaker Server Help.');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (148, 'en', 4, 'notes', 'Notes', '-
You must specify a target variable or field. If Target is not specified, this script step returns an error code that can be captured with the Get(LastError) function.');
INSERT INTO "script_step_sections" ("script_step_id", "locale", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (148, 'en', 5, 'ref-example1', 'Example 1', 'Configures an AI account, goes to the Meeting Details layout, then uses the model to get embedding vectors for the text in the Meetings::Note field in the current record and stores it as binary data in the Meetings::Note_Embedding container field.

Copy

Configure AI Account [ Account Name: "my-account" ; Model Provider: OpenAI ; API key: "sk-RZCtpWT..." ]

Go to Layout [ "Meeting Details" (Meetings) ; Animation: None ]

Insert Embedding [ Account Name: "my-account" ; Embedding Model: "text-embedding-3-small" ; Input: Meetings::Note ; Target: Meetings::Note_Embedding ]');
